After a long absence from the Lojban community (I blame the stress of
MIT), I'm back.

I've gotten rustier with my Lojban since I last actively used it, of
course. Also, I used to check my Lojban and look up words I didn't
know with a bunch of Perl, Python, and shell scripts built around
jbofihe and the wordlists; I've changed my computer environment enough
since then that conglomeration of hacks doesn't work anymore. So now I
feel like I'm flying blind when I try to write in Lojban.

So my question to the community is: how do you check your Lojban and
look up words now? Is jbofihe still the command line tool of choice?
Is there a shiny Web interface to all of this?

-- Rob


